## 2. Google Cloud Platform (GCP)

### Best Practices
* Attach service accounts directly to Compute Engine, Cloud Run, or GKE workloads instead of exporting JSON keys.
* Use **Workload Identity Federation (WIF)** for external CI/CD pipelines (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI) instead of storing service account keys in repository secrets.

### Step-by-Step Setup (CLI)

**Prerequisites:** `gcloud` CLI installed, authenticated, and target project selected (`gcloud config set project PROJECT_ID`).

```bash
# 1. Create a dedicated service account
gcloud iam service-accounts create app-backend-sa \
    --display-name="Backend Application Service Account" \
    --description="Used by backend API to read Cloud Storage objects"

# 2. Grant least-privilege IAM role scoped to a specific resource (e.g., a bucket)
gcloud storage buckets add-iam-policy-binding gs://YOUR_BUCKET_NAME \
    --member="serviceAccount:app-backend-sa@PROJECT_://gserviceaccount.com" \
    --role="roles/storage.objectViewer"

# 3. Attach to a workload (Example: Cloud Run) instead of creating a JSON key
gcloud run services update YOUR_SERVICE_NAME \
    --service-account="app-backend-sa@PROJECT_://gserviceaccount.com" \
    --region="us-central1"

# 4. Verification: Confirm IAM policy binding and active status
gcloud iam service-accounts describe app-backend-sa@PROJECT_://gserviceaccount.com
```

